#
# ------------------------------------
# CLOUDHUB DEPLOYMENT CONFIGURATION
# ------------------------------------
#
# Logs and traces of a CloudHub app go to the platform through its APISIX gateway. Log4j and the
# OpenTelemetry agent read SYSTEM properties, so the observability settings below are set in CloudHub
# Runtime Manager > the application > Settings > Properties (they become system properties) -- not in a
# properties file inside the app. <gateway> = the public host of the platform's APISIX.
#
# Prerequisites on the platform side:
#   - a certificate CloudHub trusts on the gateway (setup-letsencrypt.sh); the local CA from a fresh install
#     is not trusted by CloudHub's JVM
#   - ports 9443 (HTTPS, traces) and 9100 (TCP, logs) reachable from CloudHub (allow its egress IPs)
#   - LOG_INGEST_TOKEN and OTLP_INGEST_TOKEN from the platform's .env
#
# ---------------- Set in CloudHub > Properties ----------------
#
# Logs: JSON over TCP to Fluent Bit via APISIX's stream proxy (log4j2.xml "logs" appender)
#   logs.host=<gateway>
#   logs.port=9100
#   logs.token=<LOG_INGEST_TOKEN>
#
# Traces: OTLP/HTTP via APISIX (/otlp -> Jaeger), token header checked by the gateway
#   otel.exporter.otlp.endpoint=https://<gateway>:9443/otlp
#   otel.exporter.otlp.protocol=http/protobuf
#   otel.exporter.otlp.headers=x-otlp-token=<OTLP_INGEST_TOKEN>
#   otel.traces.exporter=otlp
#   otel.metrics.exporter=none
#   otel.logs.exporter=none
#   otel.resource.attributes=deployment.environment=cloudhub,worker.id=cloudhub
#   otel.traces.sampler=parentbased_traceidratio
#   otel.traces.sampler.arg=0.1        (10% of requests; 1.0 = all)
#
# The service name in Jaeger is the app name (tracer.xml), version = ce.version.
#
# ---------------- App configuration (this file, mule_env=cloudhub) ----------------
http.port=8081
https.port=8082
